01:02:09,000 --> 01:02:15,000
Billy Lynn's Long Halftime Walk is a 2016 war drama film directed by Ang Lee and written by
Jean-Christophe Castelli, based on the 2012 novel of the same name by Ben Fountain.

12
01:07:48,000 --> 01:07:54,000
The film stars Joe Alwyn, Garrett Hedlund, Kristen Stewart,
Vin Diesel, Steve Martin, and Chris Tucker.

13
01:13:27,000 --> 01:13:33,000
Principal photography began in April 2015 in Georgia.

14
01:19:06,000 --> 01:19:12,000
The film is a co-production between the United
States, the United Kingdom, and China.

15
01:24:45,000 --> 01:24:51,000
The film had its world premiere at the 54th New York Film Festival on October 14, 2016, and was
theatrically released in North America on November 11, 2016, by TriStar Pictures.

16
01:30:24,000 --> 01:30:30,000
It had high production costs associated with being the first-ever feature film using an extra-high frame
rate of 120 frames per second, further complicated by the 3D format, at 4K UHD resolution.

17
01:36:03,000 --> 01:36:09,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and it grossed $31
million worldwide against its $40 million budget.

18
01:41:42,000 --> 01:41:48,000
The film explores themes of post-traumatic stress disorder (ptsd), based on
novel or book, war veteran, american football, thanksgiving.

